 "notes": "Curve traced from the vector PDF of Fig. 3 (top panel, limit_combine_v2.pdf in the e-print): the black line, which the caption defines as the +/-250-bin average of the red spiky 95%-CL limit on the axion-neutron coupling g_ann (~1.5 million test frequencies over 4.5-15.5 Hz). Axes calibrated from tick-mark segments (x linear in fa [Hz], 34.60 pt/Hz anchored at 5 Hz; y log, 49.40 pt/decade anchored at 1e-10 GeV^-1) and cross-checked against the top ma axis (2-6 x 10^-14 eV). Paper defines H = g_aNN grad(a).sigma_N with g_ann in GeV^-1 (Eq. 6); converted to the canonical dimensionless coupling via g_an = 2 m_n g_ann with m_n = 0.9396 GeV (task-card 2m_N rule). Neutron limit chosen as the main result (presented first; proton limit g_app in the lower panel is the secondary scenario, derived with xi_n=0.58, xi_p=0.04 spin fractions of 21Ne, setting the other coupling to zero). Mass from m_a = h f. rho_DM = 0.4 GeV/cm^3 assumed in the Methods. Curve downsampled by RDP to 100 points; the scalloped per-scan resonance structure is preserved approximately, individual narrow spikes of the red line are averaged out by construction.",
